BACKGROUND

A. The Company has developed certain speech synthesis models, source code, and related materials for its Kova TTS product, which it wishes to make available to the public for research and non-commercial use on the terms of this Agreement.

B. As of the effective date of this Agreement, the models described in paragraph A above are based solely on synthetic training data and do not incorporate any voice recording, biometric data, or other personal information of any identifiable natural person.

C. Capitalized terms used in this Agreement have the meanings given in Section 1 below or, in the case of "Agreement", "You", "Licensee", and "Company", in the paragraph above.

1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Derivative Model" means any model, checkpoint, adapter, or other machine learning artifact created by modifying, fine-tuning, distilling, quantizing, merging, or otherwise adapting the Model Weights, in whole or in part. For clarity, Derivative Model does not include Output.

1.2 "Distribute" means to make the Model Materials or a Derivative Model available to any third party, whether by upload, transfer, publication, hosting on a public or private repository, or any other means.

1.3 "Documentation" means any manuals, specifications, release notes, or other materials describing the installation, configuration, or use of the Model Materials, made available by the Company.

1.4 "Model Materials" means, collectively, the Model Weights, the Software, and the Documentation made available by the Company as part of the "kova-tts-1-os" package, currently published at https://huggingface.co/kova-ai/kova-tts-1, together with any updates the Company may make available for that package from time to time.

1.5 "Model Weights" means the trained parameters, checkpoints, and related model files made available by the Company as part of the Model Materials.

1.6 "Non-Commercial Purpose" means any use of the Model Materials, a Derivative Model, or any Output that is not intended for, or directed toward, commercial advantage, revenue generation, or monetary compensation, and that does not form part of a live, revenue-generating, or customer-facing product or service. For clarity, Non-Commercial Purpose does not include (a) using the Model Materials, any Output, or any Derivative Model to develop, train, fine-tune, distill, or otherwise improve any other text-to-speech or voice synthesis model intended for commercial use, or (b) any revenue-generating activity, including a project funded in whole or in part by a government grant that generates revenue.

1.7 "Output" means any audio, text, or other content generated through the use of the Model Materials.

1.8 "Research Purpose" means academic, scientific, or technical research, testing, benchmarking, and evaluation of the Model Materials, a Derivative Model, or any Output, including internal evaluation by an organization to assess the potential fit, integration, or performance of the Model Materials, a Derivative Model, or any Output for a possible future application.

1.9 "Software" means the source code, scripts, and other software tools made available by the Company as part of the Model Materials.

1.10 "Training Data" means recordings, audio, transcripts, annotations, datasets, or other source materials used to train, evaluate, or develop the Model Weights.

1.11 Other Defined Terms. The terms "Agreement", "You", "Licensee", and "Company" have the meanings given to them in the preamble above.

