8. ACCEPTABLE USE

8.1 You will not, and will not permit any other person to, use the Model Materials, any Derivative Model, or any Output to:

(a) generate audio that impersonates, or is reasonably likely to be mistaken for, a specific identifiable individual, or that clones or replicates the voice of any individual, without that individual’s prior, informed, and verifiable consent;

(b) create, facilitate, or distribute fraudulent, deceptive, or misleading content, including scams, phishing, fraudulent robocalls, or content intended to circumvent voice based authentication or biometric security;

(c) generate content that exploits, or facilitates the exploitation of, minors;

(d) create or distribute synthetic audio constituting non-consensual intimate or sexually exploitative content, unlawful harassment or stalking, a credible threat of violence, or extortion or blackmail;

(e) misrepresent synthetically generated audio as a recording of a live human being, where such misrepresentation is prohibited by, or where a disclosure is required under, applicable law;

(f) create materially deceptive synthetic audio falsely presented as the authentic speech of a real public official, candidate, journalist, or other identifiable public figure, where the purpose or reasonably foreseeable effect is to deceive the public regarding a material statement or event;

(g) violate any applicable law, or infringe any intellectual property, privacy, or other right of any third party; or

(h) use the Model Materials, any Output, or any Derivative Model to develop, train, fine-tune, distill, or otherwise improve a competing commercial text-to-speech or voice synthesis model, except as expressly permitted under a separate written commercial license from the Company.

